returns":{"_0":"Strategy struct."}},"removeStrategy(address)":{"details":"A faulty strategy that has an allocated amount can not be removed, instead the strategy status      should be set as `EMERGENCY` using `toggleStrategyEmergencyStatus()`.      The address with `EULER_EARN_MANAGER` role need to manually opt-out from/disable the removed strategy rewards.","params":{"_strategy":"Address of the strategy to remove."}},"setStrategyCap(address,uint16)":{"details":"By default, cap is set to 0.","params":{"_cap":"Cap amount","_strategy":"Strategy address."}},"toggleStrategyEmergencyStatus(address)":{"details":"This should be used as a circuit-breaker to exclude a faulty strategy from being harvest or rebalanced.      It also deducts all the deposited amounts into the strategy as loss, and uses a loss socialization mechanism.      This is needed, in case the EulerEarn Vault can no longer withdraw from a certain strategy.      In the case of switching a strategy from Emergency to Active again, the max withdrawable amount from the strategy      will be set as the allocated amount, and will be immediately available to gulp.      When toggling a strategy from `Active` to `Emergency`, the strategy allocated amount will be instantly deducted as loss.      In the case of loss socialization across deposits, the vault's share price will drop instantly. Therefore, Euler Earn shares should never be used as collateral in any other protocol.      The address with `EULER_EARN_MANAGER` role need to manually opt-out from/disable the rewards of the strategy that was set in `Emergency` status.","params":{"_strategy":"Strategy address."}},"totalAllocationPoints()":{"returns":{"_0":"Total allocation points."}}},"version":1},"userdoc":{"kind":"user","methods":{"EVC()":{"notice":"Returns the address of the Ethereum Vault Connector (EVC) used by this contract."},"addStrategy(address,uint256)":{"notice":"Add new strategy with its allocation points."},"adjustAllocationPoints(address,uint256)":{"